{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C headers and implementation for image loading (stb_image.h)", "description": "This file is a single-header C library providing image loading functionality supporting multiple formats such as JPEG, PNG, BMP, GIF, TGA, PSD, HDR, and PNM. It includes API functions for loading images from memory, files, or callbacks, supports 8-bit, 16-bit, and float data, and allows configuration for flip, unpremultiplied alpha, and HDR processing. The content includes license info, usage instructions, format support, and implementation code sections.", "external_files": ["stdio.h", "stdlib.h", "string.h", "limits.h", "math.h", "stdint.h"], "external_methods": ["fread", "fseek", "ftell", "feof", "ungetc", "ferror"], "published": ["stbi_load", "stbi_image_free", "stbi_info", "stbi_is_hdr", "stbi_loadf", "stbi_set_flip_vertically_on_load", "stbi_convert_iphone_png_to_rgb"], "classes": [], "methods": [{"name": "stbi_load", "description": "Loads an image file from a filename, returning pixel data with specified channels."}, {"name": "stbi_image_free", "description": "Frees the memory allocated for an image."}, {"name": "stbi_info", "description": "Retrieves image dimensions and channels without fully decoding."}, {"name": "stbi_is_hdr", "description": "Checks if an image file is in HDR format."}, {"name": "stbi_loadf", "description": "Loads an HDR image as float data."}, {"name": "stbi_set_flip_vertically_on_load", "description": "Sets whether the image should be flipped vertically during load."}, {"name": "stbi_set_flip_vertically_on_load", "description": "Configures whether images should be flipped vertically during load."}, {"name": "stbi__bitcount", "description": "Counts the number of set bits in an unsigned int, used for mask analysis."}, {"name": "stbi__shiftsigned", "description": "Extracts an aligned N-bit value from a variable, expands it to 8-bit range."}, {"name": "stbi__bmp_set_mask_defaults", "description": "Sets default masks for differen